<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/EstuaryManagementUnits/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:A02::EstuaryManagementUnits";
        dc:date                "2011-08-15 11:58:51.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:A02::EstuaryManagementUnits";
        pav:authoredOn         "2011-08-15 11:58:51.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/EstuaryManagementUnits/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A01/current/Mitigation_Strategies_and_Preparedness/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A03/current/EstuaryManagementPlans/>;
        skos:definition        "Estuary plans divide each estuary into a number of different zones or areas called management units. Management units are discrete geographic areas, defined by biophysical characteristics and features, within which particular uses and activities are promoted, encouraged, protected, or enhanced, and others are discouraged, restricted, or prohibited. Estuary plans identify appropriate uses for each estuary management unit. Goals 16 directs what kinds of areas are to be included in each management unit and what kinds of uses can be allowed in each type of management unit."@en;
        skos:definition        "Les plans d'estuaire divisent chaque estuaire en un certain nombre de zones ou d'aires distinctes appelées unités de gestion. Les unités de gestion sont des zones géographiques discrètes, définies par des caractéristiques et des traits biophysiques, au sein desquelles certains usages et activités sont promus, encouragés, protégés ou valorisés, et d'autres découragés, restreints ou interdits. Les plans d'estuaire identifient les usages appropriés pour chaque unité de gestion d'estuaire. L'objectif 16 indique quels types de zones doivent être incluses dans chaque unité de gestion et quels types d'usages peuvent être permis dans chaque type d'unité de gestion."@fr ;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/ICANCOERO/current/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/OCACETHES/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:A02::EstuaryManagementUnits";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Estuary Management Units"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "Unités de gestion d'estuaire"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/TowBoatLanes/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:A02::TowBoatLanes";
        dc:date                "2011-08-15 11:58:51.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:A02::TowBoatLanes";
        pav:authoredOn         "2011-08-15 11:58:51.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/TowBoatLanes/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A01/current/Mitigation_Strategies_and_Preparedness/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A03/current/Navigation/>;
        skos:definition        "Lanes of mutually agreed upon tow lane areas, as agreed by Tow boat operators and local fixed gear fishermen. Prior to the establishment of such lanes it was not uncommon for tugs to collide with crabbing gear, causing damage to hulls and propulsion systems and losses of costly crab pots."@en;
        skos:definition        "Voies formant des corridors de remorquage mutuellement convenus, convenus par les opérateurs de remorqueurs et les pêcheurs à engins fixes locaux. Avant l'établissement de telles voies, il n'était pas rare que les remorqueurs entrent en collision avec l'engin de crabe, causant des dommages aux coques et aux systèmes de propulsion ainsi que la perte de casiers de crabe coûteux."@fr ;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/ICANCOERO/current/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/OCACETHES/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:A02::TowBoatLanes";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Tow Boat Lanes"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "Voies de remorquage"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A02/current/Military/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
